# Line endings for the files that run on the device.
#
# A CRLF in a device shell script is silent and total. busybox reads the
# carriage return as part of the command name, so every line fails with
# "not found" and the script exits 127. At boot that means a service never
# starts, and the only symptom is a port that does not answer. Nothing is
# logged that names the cause.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows checkout produces exactly that, so the rule
# below pins the working-tree ending for these paths whatever the local setting
# is. It deliberately does not cover the whole repository: `support/` carries
# sources committed with CRLF, and renormalising them would rewrite files this
# repository does not own.

kvmapp/system/init.d/*      text eol=lf
kvmapp/system/*.py          text eol=lf
kvmapp/system/*.sh          text eol=lf
kvmapp/jpg_stream/*         text eol=lf
kvmapp/picoclaw/**/*.sh     text eol=lf
kvmapp/picoclaw/**/*.md     text eol=lf
kvmapp/picoclaw/**/*.yaml   text eol=lf
tools/**/*.sh               text eol=lf
tools/zram/S01zram          text eol=lf
tools/slots/*.inc           text eol=lf
tools/slots/*.its.in        text eol=lf
*.sh                        text eol=lf

# Device payloads that must stay byte-exact.
*.ko                        binary
*.so                        binary
*.so.*                      binary
kvmapp/kvm_system/*         binary
kvmapp/kvm_new_app          binary
